@page "/"
@inject IDemoCatalog Catalog

<PageTitle>FlociLab</PageTitle>

<h1>FlociLab</h1>

<p class="lede">
    One official SDK per service, run against the Floci emulators. The comparison pages run the
    same operation on every cloud that has an analog. Each sample is a Razor Class Library with
    one cloud package, and a <code>lab.cs</code> beside it that runs that sample's own round-trip.
</p>

<div class="toolbar">
    <a class="button" href="/coverage">Coverage matrix</a>
    <a class="button" href="/differences">Known differences</a>
</div>

<h2>Where things stand</h2>

<table class="grid">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Cloud</th>
            <th>Samples</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        @foreach (ProviderDemos group in this.Catalog.ByProvider)
        {
            <tr>
                <td>@group.DisplayName</td>
                <td class="numeric">@group.Demos.Count</td>
            </tr>
        }
        <tr>
            <td>Total</td>
            <td class="numeric">@this.Catalog.Demos.Count</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Compare the same operation</h2>

<ul>
    <li><a href="/compare/object-storage">Object storage</a> — S3, Blob, GCS, OCI Object Storage</li>
    <li><a href="/compare/queues">Queues</a> — SQS, Queue Storage, Service Bus, Pub/Sub, OCI Queue</li>
    <li><a href="/compare/secrets">Secrets</a> — Secrets Manager, Key Vault, Secret Manager, OCI Vault Secrets</li>
    <li><a href="/compare/document-db">Document DB</a> — DynamoDB, Cosmos DB, Firestore</li>
    <li><a href="/compare/key-management">Key management</a> — KMS, Key Vault Keys, Cloud KMS, OCI Vault</li>
</ul>

<h2>The emulators</h2>

<table class="grid">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Cloud</th>
            <th>Image</th>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>AWS</td><td><code>floci/floci</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4566</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Azure</td><td><code>floci/floci-az</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4577</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>GCP</td><td><code>floci/floci-gcp</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4588</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>OCI</td><td><code>floci/floci-oci</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4599</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">
    The AppHost also starts the <a href="http://127.0.0.1:4500" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Floci
    web console</a> on port 4500. From floci-ui 0.6.0 it covers AWS, Azure, GCP and OCI. It is a
    separate product: this app is the .NET round-trip, and the side-by-side one.
</p>

<p class="note">
    Endpoints come from the <code>Floci</code> configuration section. Running under the Aspire
    AppHost overrides them with the live container endpoints; running inside the Compose network
    means setting <code>Floci__Aws__Endpoint=http://floci:4566</code> and friends.
</p>
